The derived state tables in Data/ are reductions of public records published
by the Pennsylvania Department of Environmental Protection, the Ohio
Department of Natural Resources, the New Mexico Oil Conservation Division and
the Colorado Energy and Carbon Management Commission. Those agencies' own
terms govern their raw files; this licence covers the code in this deposit and
the derived tables built from them, which are our processing and not verbatim
agency files. `SOURCES.md` records the origin of each of the 82 raw inputs and
`DATA_DICTIONARY.md` distinguishes our processing from the agency's for every
column.

Cite as:

  Alrawi, B., Huang, W., Mao, X., 2026. Derived tables and analysis code for
  "Group-identifier leakage in unconventional production models: ordinary
  covariates identify the well pad". Zenodo.
  https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22998446
